;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: flight-stream.gc
;; name in dgo: flight-stream
;; dgos: GAME

;; LIGHT JAK IN JAK 1, the flight streamer: the Jak 1 fork of Dark Flight / True Flight's map-based streamer
;; (jak2/jak3 engine/target/flight-stream.gc). Same design and the same fs- names; what Jak 1 doesn't have is gone
;; (borrow, alias and master levels, the C++ fr3 pre-warm and DGO drain, the flight wall) and what it does differently
;; is here (two level slots, want-levels with two names, want-vis by nickname, its collision probe). The Jak 1 facts and
;; the engine hooks are in flight-stream-h.gc, as in Jak 2/3; this file is not shared byte for byte, but its knobs keep
;; the Jak 2/3 values where the rule is the same (fs-lint.py checks them).
;;
;; Jak 1 loads levels when Jak's (or the camera's) path crosses a load boundary (load-boundary-data.gc): 2D lines with
;; a top and a bottom plane. A crossing only counts between the planes, and many tops are under 60 m, so a flight over
;; a line, or around its end, never loads the next level: flown to at 30 m/s, the jungle never loaded and Misty never
;; loaded and Jak died at the death line (measured on the Deck, 2026-11-19). flight-map.gc records which level owns the
;; ground of each 16 m cell of the outdoor world and how high that ground is; while flying, the level under Jak and the
;; level under the point he reaches in a few seconds are looked up there and kept loaded and displayed.
;;
;; Rules (numbered as in the Jak 2/3 file; 5 and 10 have no Jak 1 counterpart):
;;  1. "here" = the level whose ground is under Jak (fs-map-at); "next" = the first other level on the path ahead,
;;     walked cell by cell over the look-ahead distance. Jak 1 holds two levels, so here + next is the whole set.
;;     From cruise height Jak sees further than two levels reach: the area beyond them shows black until it loads (the
;;     2-slot limit; at turbo speed over Fire Canyon's end, Rock Village appears ~5 s after the hills, 2026-11-19).
;;  2. Wanted = an unmapped level Jak is inside of (an interior: its own doors brought it in, and he may fly in it),
;;     then here, then next. With nothing new ahead the last "next" stays (no reload with every wobble near a
;;     border); with no next at all, the level just left while it's still loaded.
;;  3. A new "next" further than *fs-stream-near* cells off must hold *fs-stream-settle* decisions (the far end of
;;     the path sweeps across borders as Jak turns).
;;  4. Where the map has no ground under Jak and none ahead, nothing is decided: unmapped places (the interiors under
;;     the world, the caves, the citadel) are left to the game's own boundaries.
;;  6. No vis while flying. The two loaded levels share one IOP vis buffer, and the vis nickname says whose it is;
;;     from the air the camera is where nobody walks, and a VIS loaded there crashed the game a few seconds later,
;;     four times, at Rock Village with Fire Canyon still loaded (2026-11-19), once even after the landing when the
;;     mod set the nickname itself. So from takeoff every level draws from its all-visible list (*artist-all-visible*,
;;     the debug menu's "All Visible": no vis decompression, no VIS loads) and the nickname is cleared and held
;;     (want-vis, load-boundary.gc).
;;     The landing (fs-land): on foot the game's own lines switch a level off as Jak walks away from it, but a flight
;;     crosses those lines above their tops, so a level the game never shows from where he comes down stayed on.
;;     Landing on Rock Village's pad with Fire Canyon still displayed crashed the game 1-3 s later, every time, as soon
;;     as vis came back (it births and draws by vis; the call landed in level data; 2026-11-19), while a towed landing
;;     there, after which the game had switched Fire Canyon off, was fine. So at the landing every loaded level but the
;;     one under Jak stops being displayed (it stays loaded), except after a hop, when what the game showed at the
;;     takeoff is put back. A hidden level shows again as soon as Jak is over its ground or heading onto it, a few
;;     strides ahead (fs-after-landing: a level takes a moment to get its collision back, and swimming from Sandover's
;;     water into the jungle's dropped Jak through the river before it had, 2026-11-19). The hold
;;     ends once the camera is inside one displayed level only (fs-vis-settle); then the all-visible switch goes off
;;     and vis comes back with the first vis line the game's own boundaries cross (until then a level with no vis for
;;     the camera's spot draws everything: update-visible, cam-update.gc). The checkpoint, which normally follows the
;;     vis level, is set at the landing to the nearest one of the level under Jak.
;;  7. Anti-abyss net: when the game is about to kill Jak for falling out of the world after flying, he goes back above
;;     the last spot where a ray straight down hit ground (a spot saved in the same unbroken flight never goes stale).
;;     Jak 1 also arms it on foot while a level the landing hid is still hidden, or was shown again moments ago, and has
;;     ground in Jak's column: a fall through it (no collision while it isn't displayed) puts him back on the last
;;     ground he stood on. Anywhere else a real pit is a real pit.
;;  8. With solid ground right below a flying Jak, the game's death line doesn't apply (the death line is the
;;     checkpoint level's: Snowy's is at +128 m, over ground 100 m lower in the neighbouring pass).
;;  9. Never fight the game for the level list: if the wants get changed back more than a few times a second, the
;;     streamer backs off for 5 s.
;; Hooks (LIGHT JAK, declared in flight-stream-h.gc): want-levels (load-boundary.gc) calls *fs-want-levels-hook*, so a
;; boundary crossed in flight is re-decided in the same frame; the endless-fall checks (logic-target.gc, collide-shape.gc)
;; ask *fs-endlessfall-hook* first; want-vis is held by *fs-vis-hold?*. From light-flight.gc: fs-tick while flying,
;; fs-land at the landing, fs-after-landing from Jak's post (lj-post) every frame he runs.
;; Lint: lj-lint.py and fs-lint.py.

;; ---- LEVEL STREAMING WHILE FLYING ----
(define *fs-stream-timer* 0)                ;; frames since the last decision
(define *fs-stream-ahead* 3.5)              ;; seconds of flight the next level is picked ahead...
(define *fs-stream-ahead-min* (meters 100)) ;; ...at least this far, at most *fs-stream-ahead-max*
(define *fs-stream-ahead-max* (meters 250)) ;; (the path is walked cell by cell, so no neighbour is skipped)
(define *fs-stream-settle* 3)               ;; decisions in a row a far "next" needs before it counts...
(define *fs-stream-near* 3)                 ;; ...one whose ground starts within this many cells counts at once
(define *fs-stream-every* 6)                ;; frames between decisions
(define *fs-map-below* (meters 15))         ;; Jak may be this far under a cell's ground and still be "over" it
(define *fs-map-ahead-below* (meters 60))   ;; ...and the ground ahead may be this much higher than Jak
(define *fs-air-frame* 0)                   ;; last frame the flight code ran (the want hook checks it)
(define *fs-stream-now* #f)                 ;; the level Jak is over
(define *fs-stream-next* #f)                ;; the level he's heading for
(define *fs-stream-cand* #f)                ;; the "next" being considered, and for how long
(define *fs-stream-cand-n* 0)
(define *fs-stream-last-frame* 0)           ;; when the last decision ran
(define *fs-stream-prev* #f)                ;; the level Jak just left (kept until a new "next" shows up)
(define *fs-stream-fight-frame* 0)          ;; rule 9: start of the current one-second window...
(define *fs-stream-fight-n* 0)              ;; ...and how often the wants were re-issued in it
(define *fs-stream-fight-max* 4)
(define *fs-stream-backoff-until* 0)        ;; no decisions before this frame
(define *fs-in-want-hook?* #f)              ;; our own want-levels must not re-enter the hook
(define *fs-vis-off-in-air?* #t)            ;; rule 6
(define *fs-hook-window* (seconds 0.2))     ;; a want-levels this soon after a flight tick, still flying, is re-decided
                                            ;; (the Jak 2/3 file's inline 60 ticks)
(define *fs-probe-radius* 40.96)            ;; the ground ray's sphere (as the Jak 2/3 streamer's)
(define *fs-rescue-window* (seconds 10))    ;; the abyss net only acts this soon after a flight (Jak 2/3: inline)
(define *fs-flight-gap* (seconds 0.1))      ;; flight ticks further apart than this: a new flight began
(define *fs-land-frame* 0)                  ;; the last landing (fs-land)
(define *fs-vis-landed?* #f)                ;; landed, the vis hold not yet ended (rule 6)
(define *fs-hidden-level* (the-as symbol #f)) ;; the loaded level the landing stopped displaying, until it shows again
(define *fs-shown-level* (the-as symbol #f))  ;; ...and once shown again, for *fs-show-grace* (its collision may lag)
(define *fs-shown-frame* 0)
(define *fs-show-grace* (seconds 5))
(define *fs-show-ahead* (meters 24))         ;; it shows again when Jak's path this far ahead is over its ground
(define *fs-hop-dist* (meters 40))          ;; a landing this close (flat) to the takeoff is a hop (rule 6)
(define *fs-takeoff-pos* (new 'static 'vector)) ;; where the flight began...
(define *fs-takeoff-shown0* (the-as symbol #f)) ;; ...and the wanted levels the game displayed then
(define *fs-takeoff-shown1* (the-as symbol #f))
(defconstant FS-MAP-FLOOR (meters 130))     ;; the map's byte encoding: (height + FS-MAP-FLOOR) / 2 m + 1 (mapgen.py)
(defconstant FS-MAP-STEP (meters 2))

(defmacro fs-now ()
  "The real frame counter (300 ticks a second; it runs through pauses, as the Jak 2/3 file's real-clock)."
  `(-> *display* real-frame-counter))

(defun fs-floor ((v float))
  "floor, as an int (Jak 1 has none for floats)"
  (let ((i (the int v)))
    (if (< v (the float i)) (+ i -1) i)))

(defun fs-mapped? ((name symbol))
  "Is this level in the ground map?"
  (let ((yes #f))
    (dotimes (i (-> *fs-map-names* length))
      (if (= (-> *fs-map-names* i) name) (set! yes #t)))
    yes))

(defun fs-level-status ((name symbol))
  "The status of loaded level NAME, or 'inactive."
  (let ((st 'inactive))
    (dotimes (i FS-LEVELS)
      (let ((lv (-> *level* level i)))
        (if (and (= (-> lv name) name) (!= (-> lv status) 'inactive)) (set! st (-> lv status)))))
    st))

(defun fs-level-present? ((name symbol))
  "Is this level wanted or loaded right now?"
  (let ((yes (!= (fs-level-status name) 'inactive)))
    (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
      (if (= (-> *load-state* want i name) name) (set! yes #t)))
    yes))

(defun fs-map-byte ((i int) (pos vector))
  "Mapped level I's byte for the cell under pos: 0 = no ground there, else (height + FS-MAP-FLOOR) / FS-MAP-STEP + 1."
  (let* ((d (* i 5))
         (ix (- (fs-floor (/ (-> pos x) FS-MAP-CELL)) (-> *fs-map-dims* d)))
         (iz (- (fs-floor (/ (-> pos z) FS-MAP-CELL)) (-> *fs-map-dims* (+ d 1))))
         (nx (-> *fs-map-dims* (+ d 2))))
    (if (and (>= ix 0) (>= iz 0) (< ix nx) (< iz (-> *fs-map-dims* (+ d 3))))
      (the-as int (-> *fs-map-cells* (+ (-> *fs-map-dims* (+ d 4)) (* iz nx) ix)))
      0)))

(defun fs-map-at ((pos vector) (below float))
  "The mapped level whose ground is under pos, or #f. Where two levels have ground in the cell, the higher one.
   Ground more than BELOW above pos doesn't count (in a cave or an interior under the world, Jak is not over the
   level above him)."
  (let ((top (+ 1 (the int (/ (+ (-> pos y) below FS-MAP-FLOOR) FS-MAP-STEP))))
        (best (the-as symbol #f))
        (bestb 0))
    (dotimes (i (-> *fs-map-names* length))
      (let ((b (fs-map-byte i pos)))
        (when (and (< 0 b) (<= b top) (< bestb b))
          (set! best (-> *fs-map-names* i))
          (set! bestb b))))
    best))

(defun fs-map-has? ((name symbol) (pos vector))
  "Does mapped level NAME have ground anywhere in the cell under pos (at any height)?"
  (let ((yes #f))
    (dotimes (i (-> *fs-map-names* length))
      (if (and (= (-> *fs-map-names* i) name) (< 0 (fs-map-byte i pos))) (set! yes #t)))
    yes))

(defun fs-want-display ((name symbol))
  "NAME's display setting in the load state ('display, #f, ...), or 'none when it isn't wanted at all."
  (let ((d 'none))
    (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
      (if (= (-> *load-state* want i name) name) (set! d (-> *load-state* want i display?))))
    d))

(defun fs-inside-level? ((name symbol) (pos vector))
  "Is pos inside level NAME's bounding sphere (level-info)? A level without one never counts as entered."
  (let ((info (lookup-level-info name)))
    (and info
         (nonzero? (-> info bsphere))
         (-> info bsphere)
         (< 0.0 (-> info bsphere w))
         (< (vector-vector-distance pos (the-as vector (-> info bsphere))) (-> info bsphere w)))))

(defun fs-keep-slot ((k0 symbol) (k1 symbol) (nm symbol))
  "Where NM goes in the keep pair: 0, 1, or -1 (no name, already in, or full)."
  (cond
    ((or (not nm) (= nm k0) (= nm k1)) -1)
    ((not k0) 0)
    ((not k1) 1)
    (else -1)))

(defun fs-stream-decide ()
  "Pick the levels to keep loaded and re-issue the wants if they differ from what's wanted now."
  (when (and *target* (< *fs-stream-backoff-until* (fs-now)))
    (let* ((pos (-> *target* control trans))
           (v (-> *target* control transv))
           (sp (vector-xz-length v))
           (ahead (new-stack-vector0))
           (frame (fs-now))
           (here (fs-map-at pos *fs-map-below*))
           (next (the-as symbol #f))
           (near? #f))
      ;; after a teleport or a long walk the remembered levels are stale: forget them
      (when (< (seconds 2) (- frame *fs-stream-last-frame*))
        (set! *fs-stream-cand* #f)
        (set! *fs-stream-next* #f)
        (set! *fs-stream-prev* #f)
        (set! *fs-stream-now* #f))
      ;; over a gap in the map (the sea, a seam between two grids): still the level just flown over
      (if (and (not here) *fs-stream-now* (fs-level-present? *fs-stream-now*)) (set! here *fs-stream-now*))
      ;; the first other level along the path ahead, cell by cell
      (when (< (meters 1) sp)
        (let ((steps (the int (/ (fmin *fs-stream-ahead-max* (fmax *fs-stream-ahead-min* (* sp *fs-stream-ahead*))) FS-MAP-CELL)))
              (dx (* (/ (-> v x) sp) FS-MAP-CELL))
              (dz (* (/ (-> v z) sp) FS-MAP-CELL)))
          (vector-copy! ahead pos)
          (dotimes (i steps)
            (set! (-> ahead x) (+ (-> ahead x) dx))
            (set! (-> ahead z) (+ (-> ahead z) dz))
            (when (not next)
              (let ((lv (fs-map-at ahead *fs-map-ahead-below*)))
                (when (and lv (!= lv here))
                  (set! next lv)
                  (set! near? (< i *fs-stream-near*))))))))
      ;; nothing new ahead (hovering, turning, slow): the level picked last stays while it's here
      (if (and (not next) *fs-stream-next* (!= *fs-stream-next* here) (fs-level-present? *fs-stream-next*))
        (set! next *fs-stream-next*))
      (when (or here next)
        (if (and here (!= here *fs-stream-now*)) (set! *fs-stream-prev* *fs-stream-now*))
        (set! *fs-stream-last-frame* frame)
        ;; a new "next" has to hold for a few decisions (the far end of the path sweeps across borders as Jak turns),
        ;; unless its ground is only a few cells off
        (cond
          ((= next *fs-stream-cand*) (set! *fs-stream-cand-n* (+ *fs-stream-cand-n* 1)))
          (else (set! *fs-stream-cand* next) (set! *fs-stream-cand-n* 1)))
        (if (and (!= next *fs-stream-next*) (not near?) (< *fs-stream-cand-n* *fs-stream-settle*) (!= *fs-stream-next* here))
          (set! next *fs-stream-next*) ;; not settled yet: keep the previous next
          (set! *fs-stream-next* next))
        (set! *fs-stream-now* here)
        ;; the two levels to keep: an unmapped wanted level Jak is inside of, then here, then next (else the level
        ;; just left, else the other mapped level already wanted)
        (let ((keep0 (the-as symbol #f))
              (keep1 (the-as symbol #f)))
          (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
            (let ((nm (-> *load-state* want i name)))
              (if (and nm (not keep0) (not (fs-mapped? nm)) (fs-inside-level? nm pos)) (set! keep0 nm))))
          (case (fs-keep-slot keep0 keep1 here) ((0) (set! keep0 here)) ((1) (set! keep1 here)))
          (case (fs-keep-slot keep0 keep1 next) ((0) (set! keep0 next)) ((1) (set! keep1 next)))
          (when (not next)
            (let ((spare (if (and *fs-stream-prev* (fs-mapped? *fs-stream-prev*) (fs-level-present? *fs-stream-prev*))
                           *fs-stream-prev*
                           (the-as symbol #f))))
              (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
                (let ((nm (-> *load-state* want i name)))
                  (if (and (not spare) nm (!= nm here) (fs-mapped? nm)) (set! spare nm))))
              (case (fs-keep-slot keep0 keep1 spare) ((0) (set! keep0 spare)) ((1) (set! keep1 spare)))))
          ;; only touch the wants when they'd change, and never without the level under Jak
          (let ((same (and (or (not keep0) (= keep0 (-> *load-state* want 0 name)) (= keep0 (-> *load-state* want 1 name)))
                           (or (not keep1) (= keep1 (-> *load-state* want 0 name)) (= keep1 (-> *load-state* want 1 name)))
                           (or (not (-> *load-state* want 0 name))
                               (= (-> *load-state* want 0 name) keep0) (= (-> *load-state* want 0 name) keep1))
                           (or (not (-> *load-state* want 1 name))
                               (= (-> *load-state* want 1 name) keep0) (= (-> *load-state* want 1 name) keep1))))
                (have-here (or (not here) (= keep0 here) (= keep1 here))))
            (when (and (not same) have-here)
              ;; rule 9: something else keeps changing the level set back: stop for a while
              (when (< (seconds 1) (- frame *fs-stream-fight-frame*))
                (set! *fs-stream-fight-frame* frame)
                (set! *fs-stream-fight-n* 0))
              (set! *fs-stream-fight-n* (+ *fs-stream-fight-n* 1))
              (when (< *fs-stream-fight-max* *fs-stream-fight-n*)
                (set! *fs-stream-backoff-until* (+ frame (seconds 5)))
                (format 0 "FS: the level set keeps being changed back, hands off for 5 s (~A ~A)~%" here next))
              (let ((was *fs-in-want-hook?*))
                (set! *fs-in-want-hook?* #t)
                (want-levels *load-state* keep0 keep1)
                (set! *fs-in-want-hook?* was))
              (if keep0 (want-display-level *load-state* keep0 'display))
              (if keep1 (want-display-level *load-state* keep1 'display))
              ;; one line per change of the level set: with the FSDUMP lines of the abyss net, the history a fall
              ;; through the world is diagnosed from
              ;; (format takes at most six arguments: two calls)
              (format 0 "LVL ~D stream ~A ~A " frame here next)
              (format 0 "keep ~A ~A ~,,0M ~,,0M~%" keep0 keep1 (-> pos x) (-> pos z)))))
        ))
    0)
  (none))

(defun fs-vis-takeoff ()
  "Rule 6, every flight tick: no vis while flying; the streamer decides what's displayed."
  (when (and *fs-vis-off-in-air?* (not *fs-vis-hold?*))
    (set! (-> *load-state* vis-nick) #f)
    (set! *artist-all-visible* #t)
    (set! *fs-vis-hold?* #t))
  (set! *fs-vis-landed?* #f)
  (set! *fs-hidden-level* #f)
  (set! *fs-shown-level* #f)
  (none))

(defun fs-set-checkpoint-near ((lv symbol) (pos vector))
  "The checkpoint to level LV's continue nearest to pos (the vis level, which it normally follows, is held)."
  (when (= (fs-level-status lv) 'active)
    (let ((info (lookup-level-info lv))
          (best (the-as continue-point #f)))
      (when info
        (let ((l (-> info continues)))
          (while (not (null? l))
            (let ((c (the-as continue-point (car l))))
              (if (and (zero? (-> c flags))
                       (or (not best) (< (vector-vector-distance pos (-> c trans)) (vector-vector-distance pos (-> best trans)))))
                (set! best c)))
            (set! l (cdr l)))))
      (if best (set-continue! *game-info* best))))
  (none))

(defun fs-land ((pos vector))
  "Rule 6, at the landing (lj-land!; also a flight ended in mid-air): every loaded mapped level but the one under Jak
   stops being displayed, unless this was a hop and the game displayed it at the takeoff; the checkpoint goes to the
   nearest one of the level under Jak; the vis hold ends later, in the settle check below."
  (set! *fs-land-frame* (fs-now))
  (when (and *fs-vis-hold?* (not *fs-vis-landed?*))
    (set! *fs-vis-landed?* #t)
    (let ((lv (fs-map-at pos *fs-map-below*))
          (hop? (< (vector-vector-xz-distance pos *fs-takeoff-pos*) *fs-hop-dist*)))
      (when lv
        (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
          (let ((nm (-> *load-state* want i name)))
            (when (and nm (!= nm lv) (fs-mapped? nm) (-> *load-state* want i display?)
                       (not (and hop? (or (= nm *fs-takeoff-shown0*) (= nm *fs-takeoff-shown1*)))))
              (format 0 "FS: landed on ~A, ~A no longer displayed~%" lv nm)
              (want-display-level *load-state* nm #f)
              (set! *fs-hidden-level* nm))))
        (fs-set-checkpoint-near lv pos))))
  (none))

(defun fs-show-hidden ((why string))
  "Display the level the landing hid again (rule 6)."
  (when *fs-hidden-level*
    (format 0 "FS: ~A displayed again (~S)~%" *fs-hidden-level* why)
    (want-display-level *load-state* *fs-hidden-level* 'display)
    (set! *fs-shown-level* *fs-hidden-level*)
    (set! *fs-shown-frame* (fs-now))
    (set! *fs-hidden-level* #f))
  (none))

(defun fs-hidden-under? ((pos vector))
  "Rule 7's on-foot arm: does the level the landing hid (or showed again moments ago) have ground in pos's column?"
  (or (and *fs-hidden-level* (fs-map-has? *fs-hidden-level* pos))
      (and *fs-shown-level*
           (< (- (fs-now) *fs-shown-frame*) *fs-show-grace*)
           (fs-map-has? *fs-shown-level* pos))))

(defun fs-camera-in-both? ()
  "Are both of Jak 1's level slots active with the camera inside both levels' boxes? (The streamer's one read of the
   camera: level-update computes inside-boxes? from *math-camera*.)"
  (let ((n 0))
    (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
      (let ((lv (-> *level* level i)))
        (if (and (= (-> lv status) 'active) (-> lv inside-boxes?)) (+! n 1))))
    (= n FS-SLOTS)))

(defun fs-vis-settle ()
  "Rule 6 after a landing: end the vis hold once the camera is inside one displayed level only."
  (when (and *fs-vis-landed?* (not (fs-camera-in-both?)))
    (set! *fs-vis-landed?* #f)
    (set! *fs-vis-hold?* #f)
    (set! *artist-all-visible* #f))
  (none))

(defun fs-stream-hook ()
  "Runs after every want-levels call (load-boundary.gc): while flying, re-decide in the same frame, so a boundary
   crossed in flight can't take the ground away. Not once he has landed: the game's own lines are in charge again
   (and re-deciding would display the level the landing hid)."
  (if (and (not *fs-in-want-hook?*)
           (< *fs-land-frame* *fs-air-frame*)
           (< (- (fs-now) *fs-air-frame*) *fs-hook-window*))
    (fs-stream-decide))
  (none))

(set! *fs-want-levels-hook* fs-stream-hook)

;; ---- ANTI-ABYSS NET (rules 7 and 8) ----
;; If the ground isn't there anyway (a level late, a place the map doesn't know), Jak falls through the world and the
;; game kills him below the checkpoint level's bottom-height ('endlessfall, logic-target.gc). That check asks
;; *fs-endlessfall-hook* first: when Jak was flying moments ago (or is falling through a level the landing hid) he is
;; put back above the last spot where a ray cast straight down hit solid ground.
(define *fs-safe-pos* (new 'static 'vector)) ;; where Jak last flew (or stood, while a level is hidden) over solid ground
(define *fs-safe-ground-y* 0.0)              ;; the height of that ground
(define *fs-safe-frame* 0)                   ;; when that was (0 = never)
(define *fs-safe-probe-frame* 0)             ;; when the ray was last cast
(define *fs-safe-probe* (meters 150))        ;; how far down the ray looks
(define *fs-safe-max-age* (seconds 20))      ;; an older spot isn't trusted (teleports, long drops)...
(define *fs-air-since* 0)                    ;; ...unless it was saved since this flight began (here)
(define *fs-safe-lift* (meters 10))          ;; Jak is put back at least this far above the ground
(define *fs-abyss-saves* 0)
(define *fs-dump-frame* 0)
(define *fs-veto-frame* 0)
(define *fs-probe-y* 0.0)                    ;; where the last ray hit

(defun fs-dump ((why string))
  "The black box: the streamer's view of the world, into the game log (at most every 5 s)."
  (let ((now (fs-now)))
    (when (and *target* (< (seconds 5) (- now *fs-dump-frame*)))
      (set! *fs-dump-frame* now)
      (let ((p (-> *target* control trans)))
        (format 0 "FSDUMP ~S frame ~D pos ~,,0M ~,,0M ~,,0M speed ~,,0M~%" why now (-> p x) (-> p y) (-> p z)
                (vector-xz-length (-> *target* control transv))))
      (format 0 "FSDUMP now ~A next ~A prev ~A current-level ~A vis ~A~%" *fs-stream-now* *fs-stream-next*
              *fs-stream-prev* (if (-> *target* current-level) (-> *target* current-level name) #f)
              (-> *load-state* vis-nick))
      (format 0 "FSDUMP hold ~A landed ~A hidden ~A artist ~A~%" *fs-vis-hold?* *fs-vis-landed?* *fs-hidden-level*
              *artist-all-visible*)
      (format 0 "FSDUMP safe ~,,0M ~,,0M ~,,0M ground ~,,0M age ~D air-age ~D~%" (-> *fs-safe-pos* x)
              (-> *fs-safe-pos* y) (-> *fs-safe-pos* z) *fs-safe-ground-y* (- now *fs-safe-frame*) (- now *fs-air-frame*))
      (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
        (if (-> *load-state* want i name)
          (format 0 "FSDUMP want ~A ~A~%" (-> *load-state* want i name) (-> *load-state* want i display?))))
      (dotimes (i FS-LEVELS)
        (if (!= (-> *level* level i status) 'inactive)
          (format 0 "FSDUMP level ~A ~A~%" (-> *level* level i name) (-> *level* level i status))))))
  (none))

(defun fs-ground-below? ((pos vector))
  "Cast a ray straight down from pos: is there solid ground no further down than *fs-safe-probe* (its height goes to
   *fs-probe-y*)?"
  (let ((start (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (dir (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (hit (new 'stack-no-clear 'collide-tri-result)))
    (set! (-> start quad) (-> pos quad))
    (+! (-> start y) (meters 1))
    (set-vector! dir 0.0 (- *fs-safe-probe*) 0.0 1.0)
    (let ((f (fill-and-probe-using-line-sphere *collide-cache* start dir *fs-probe-radius* (collide-kind background)
                                               (the-as process #f) hit (new 'static 'pat-surface :noentity #x1))))
      (cond
        ((and (<= 0.0 f) (<= f 1.0))
         (set! *fs-probe-y* (+ (-> start y) (* f (-> dir y))))
         #t)
        (else #f)))))

(defun fs-abyss-net-at ((pos vector))
  "Twice a second while flying (and standing, while a level is hidden): remember this spot if there is solid ground
   straight below."
  (let ((now (fs-now)))
    (when (< (seconds 0.5) (- now *fs-safe-probe-frame*))
      (set! *fs-safe-probe-frame* now)
      (when (fs-ground-below? pos)
        (vector-copy! *fs-safe-pos* pos)
        (set! *fs-safe-ground-y* *fs-probe-y*)
        (set! *fs-safe-frame* now))))
  (none))

(defun fs-endlessfall-rescue ((why symbol))
  "The game is about to kill Jak for falling out of the world: below the death line ('line, logic-target.gc) or onto a
   death plane ('surface, collide-shape.gc: the kill meshes under the world's edges, reached by sliding down the
   invisible walls there). If he was flying moments ago, or is falling through the level the landing hid: below the
   line with solid ground right below, it isn't a fall out of the world at all, he just lands (#t: no death; not for
   a death plane, which may be that ground). With a fresh spot over solid ground, put him back there, hovering, and
   say so (#t). Otherwise #f, and the game carries on as it always did."
  (let ((now (fs-now))
        (saved #f))
    (when (and *target*
               (or (< (- now *fs-air-frame*) *fs-rescue-window*)
                   (fs-hidden-under? (-> *target* control trans))))
      (cond
        ((and (= why 'line) (fs-ground-below? (-> *target* control trans)))
         (when (< (seconds 5) (- now *fs-veto-frame*))
           (set! *fs-veto-frame* now)
           (format 0 "FS: ground below Jak, the death line of ~A doesn't apply (~,,0M ~,,0M ~,,0M)~%"
                   (if (-> *target* current-level) (-> *target* current-level name) #f)
                   (-> *target* control trans x) (-> *target* control trans y) (-> *target* control trans z)))
         (set! saved #t))
        ((and (< 0 *fs-safe-frame*)
              (or (< (- now *fs-safe-frame*) *fs-safe-max-age*)
                  ;; saved since this flight began: still the place he flew out from
                  (<= *fs-air-since* *fs-safe-frame*)))
         (fs-dump "ABYSS")
         (let ((ctrl (-> *target* control)))
           (set! (-> ctrl trans quad) (-> *fs-safe-pos* quad))
           (set! (-> ctrl trans y) (fmax (-> *fs-safe-pos* y) (+ *fs-safe-ground-y* *fs-safe-lift*)))
           (vector-reset! (-> ctrl transv)))
         (set! *fs-abyss-saves* (+ *fs-abyss-saves* 1))
         (format 0 "ABYSS: ~A, put Jak back at ~,,0M ~,,0M ~,,0M (~D)~%" why (-> *fs-safe-pos* x) (-> *fs-safe-pos* y)
                 (-> *fs-safe-pos* z) *fs-abyss-saves*)
         (set! saved #t))
        (else (fs-dump "ABYSS-DEATH"))))
    saved))

(set! *fs-endlessfall-hook* fs-endlessfall-rescue)

(defbehavior fs-tick target ()
  "Per frame while flying: the abyss net, the level decision every few frames, and every wanted mapped level that is
   loaded but undrawn displayed (display is normally switched on by boundaries, which flight skips)."
  ;; a gap in the ticks means a new flight began (the abyss net trusts spots saved since then; rule 6 remembers where,
  ;; and what the game displayed there, before the display loop below changes it)
  (when (< *fs-flight-gap* (- (fs-now) *fs-air-frame*))
    (set! *fs-air-since* (fs-now))
    (vector-copy! *fs-takeoff-pos* (-> self control trans))
    (set! *fs-takeoff-shown0* (if (-> *load-state* want 0 display?) (-> *load-state* want 0 name) (the-as symbol #f)))
    (set! *fs-takeoff-shown1* (if (-> *load-state* want 1 display?) (-> *load-state* want 1 name) (the-as symbol #f))))
  (set! *fs-air-frame* (fs-now))
  (fs-vis-takeoff)
  (fs-abyss-net-at (-> self control trans))
  (set! *fs-stream-timer* (+ *fs-stream-timer* 1))
  (when (<= *fs-stream-every* *fs-stream-timer*)
    (set! *fs-stream-timer* 0)
    (fs-stream-decide)
    (dotimes (i FS-SLOTS)
      (let ((nm (-> *load-state* want i name)))
        (if (and nm (not (-> *load-state* want i display?)) (fs-mapped? nm))
          (want-display-level *load-state* nm 'display)))))
  (none))

(defbehavior fs-after-landing target ()
  "Every frame Jak runs (lj-post, from target-post; not while paused): rule 6 after a landing (the vis hold ends once
   safe; the level the landing hid shows again as soon as Jak is over its ground or heading onto it) and rule 7 while
   it is hidden (the ground he stands on is saved as he walks)."
  (fs-vis-settle)
  (when *fs-hidden-level*
    (let* ((pos (-> self control trans))
           (v (-> self control transv))
           (sp (vector-xz-length v))
           (ahead (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
           (d (fs-want-display *fs-hidden-level*)))
      (vector-copy! ahead pos)
      (when (< (meters 1) sp)
        (set! (-> ahead x) (+ (-> ahead x) (* (/ (-> v x) sp) *fs-show-ahead*)))
        (set! (-> ahead z) (+ (-> ahead z) (* (/ (-> v z) sp) *fs-show-ahead*))))
      (cond
        ((or (= d 'none) d) (set! *fs-hidden-level* #f)) ;; unloaded, or the game's own lines showed it
        ((or (= (fs-map-at pos *fs-map-below*) *fs-hidden-level*) (= (fs-map-at ahead *fs-map-below*) *fs-hidden-level*))
         (fs-show-hidden "Jak is heading onto it"))
        ((logtest? (-> self control status) (cshape-moving-flags onsurf)) (fs-abyss-net-at pos)))))
  (none))

(defun fs-reset! ()
  "Jak's birth (a death, a load, a new game: lj-form-spawn): a flight cut off without a landing is forgotten, vis back
   on, no level hidden (the continue's own display list applies), and no spot of the old session is trusted."
  (when *fs-vis-hold?*
    (set! *artist-all-visible* #f)
    (set! *fs-vis-hold?* #f))
  (set! *fs-vis-landed?* #f)
  (set! *fs-hidden-level* #f)
  (set! *fs-shown-level* #f)
  (set! *fs-safe-frame* 0)
  (set! *fs-air-frame* 0)
  (set! *fs-air-since* 0)
  (set! *fs-land-frame* 0)
  (none))
